==Overview==
'''Stances''' are states that grant a passive bonus to various stats or mechanics to the class that have them.

Stances available to the following classes:
* {{ClassTooltip|Ironsoul}} and {{ClassTooltip|Oni}}
* {{ClassTooltip|Abolisher}} while in [[Quasi-Realms#A Tragic Fate|A Tragic Fate Quasi-Realm]]
* {{ClassTooltip|Shapeshifter}} while in [[Quasi-Realms#Primal Instincts|Primal Instincts Quasi-Realm]]

A stance can be activated or selected by pressing its hotkey or clicking its button.

==Ironsoul and Oni==
For both of these classes, only one stance can be active at a time.

By default, the {{StanceTooltip|Meditation}} Stance is active when none is selected.

===Meditation===
{{StanceTooltip|Meditation}} Stance charges non-shard spells over time ('''X'''% per sec).

Each second, this gives:
<br><math>(\text{Charging Speed} \times X)%</math>
<br>of a charge to all Charging spells on the Spell Panel. This effect is scales with cost, so e.g. 20% per sec will always give 20% of a charge (increased by Charging Speed).

However, certain spells do not get the full benefit. While the effect still scales with cost, the charging itself is directly reduced per these formulas.

{{SpellTooltip|Synthetic Entity}}, {{SpellTooltip|Temper The Steel}}, {{SpellTooltip|Force Of Will}}, and {{SpellTooltip|Possessed Blade}} instead get:
<br><math>\frac{\text{Charging Speed} \times X}{\text{Charges} + 1} \,%</math>
<br>of a charge per sec.

{{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Furious Strike}} instead gets:
<br><math>\frac{\text{Charging Speed} \times X}{\text{Charges}^2 \times 5 + \text{Charges} \times 6 + 1} \,%</math>
<br>of a charge per sec.

Certain items can speed charging in various ways:
* {{ItemTooltip|Grasp Of The Grave}} reduces charging Spells' cost by '''5'''%. This reduces the cost of Charging spells by 5% ''additively''. '''Meditation''' charging scales with cost, so this has no effect.
* {{ItemTooltip|Spell Helix}} reduces charge Spells charging time by '''5'''%. This reduces the cost of Charging spells by 5% ''additively''. '''Meditation''' charging scales with cost, so this has no effect.
* {{ItemTooltip|Perfected Kata Bracers}} Reduces charging Spells' cost by '''25'''%. This reduces the cost of Charging spells by 25% ''multiplicatively''. '''Meditation''' charging scales with cost, so this has no effect.
* {{ItemTooltip|Temporal Scabbard}} Enchant: Increases charge-based spell charging speed by '''10'''%. This increases '''Charging Speed''' by 10% per enchant ''multiplicatively''. This ''does'' increase '''Meditation''' charging.

===Defense===
{{StanceTooltip|Defense}} Stance reduces the duration of Incantation spells by '''Y'''%. {{ClassTooltip|Oni}}: Makes Furious Strike instant.

===Berserk===
{{StanceTooltip|Berserk}} Stance increases the efficiency of Evocation spells by '''Z'''%.

==Abolisher (Quasi-Realm)==
During [[Quasi-Realms#A Tragic Fate|A Tragic Fate Quasi-Realm]], this class loses {{PetTooltip|Doppelganger}} but gains Stances as a replacement which provide passive bonuses similar to unique perks or attributes from its former pet.

By default, the class has no Stance active until one is selected.

<small>''NOTE: The information that follows was copied from [[A Tragic Fate Abolisher Guide#Explanation of the stances|A Tragic Fate Abolisher Guide]].</small>

Each stance has 3 perks associated with them, obtained at lvls 10, 20, and 30 of the respective stance. '''You do not need a stance selected to have its perks be active.''' Instead each stance always provides its passive bonuses, and selecting a stance just provides a small amount of bonus Character Ability Power to the respective perks instead. To balance this '''the exp cost of each stance is based on the total lvl of all 3 stances''', so for example if cruelty was lvl 30, but Treachery was lvl 0, lvl 1 of treachery would still cost the same as lvl 31 of cruelty. This effectively means you need to think about your final desired investment balance.

XP to reach next level:
<br><math>1.155^{L} \times 100</math>
<br>Total XP to reach Level '''n''':
<br><math>\left( 1.155^{n} - 1 \right) \times 645</math>
<br>where:
<br><math>L = \text{Current Level Sum}</math>

